            <ArticleTitle>Radiology of the month. Headache. Subdural hematoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>345-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 28-year-old woman with a three-year history of epilepsy was evaluated with intracranial monitoring, which consisted of two subdural strip electrodes and eight depth electrodes. On the third day of monitoring, she developed a headache but no focal signs or symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
